Description: text installer of Legion
 legion-install installs Legion from the live session of the USB stick on a
 disk of the computer. It erases the whole disk and creates an EFI system
 partition and a root partition, encrypted with LUKS2 if you choose it. The
 root partition gets a copy of the system from the USB stick. The installer
 asks for the language, keyboard layout, time zone, computer name, account,
 encryption and swap. It switches the keyboard of the live session to the
 chosen layout. On an encrypted disk it asks for the disk passphrase, shows
 a recovery key and can add a FIDO2 security key.
 .
 The package is meant for the live session only. The installer removes it,
 together with legion-live, from the installed system.

